    "hIz-Vz-0qf.text" : {
      "comment" : "Class = \"UILabel\"; text = \"Now you are a non-smoker and are trying to stay that way. When we make changes, it’s critical to meditate on how important this change is to you and how confident you are in making this change. You want to pay attention to how your mind, body, and emotional regulation feel differently, how your attitude changed, and what you have started doing instead for better self-care.\\n\\nThinking about it helps you to not go back to your old relationship with smoking.\\n\\nNow you know what to expect on this ride. It won’t hit you as a surprise when you expect ups and downs of this journey! Remember it’s all about coming up with a strategy that works for you, it’s not about your will power.\\n\\nAre you out of the woods? Many people want to know how long it takes before the chance of going back to tobacco is no longer a concern. Relapse most commonly happens in the first one to three months after quitting.\\n\\nHowever, it’s always wise to be on guard\"; ObjectID = \"hIz-Vz-0qf\";",
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Now you are a non-smoker and are trying to stay that way. When we make changes, it’s critical to meditate on how important this change is to you and how confident you are in making this change. You want to pay attention to how your mind, body, and emotional regulation feel differently, how your attitude changed, and what you have started doing instead for better self-care.\n\nThinking about it helps you to not go back to your old relationship with smoking.\n\nNow you know what to expect on this ride. It won’t hit you as a surprise when you expect ups and downs of this journey! Remember it’s all about coming up with a strategy that works for you, it’s not about your will power.\n\nAre you out of the woods? Many people want to know how long it takes before the chance of going back to tobacco is no longer a concern. Relapse most commonly happens in the first one to three months after quitting.\n\nHowever, it’s always wise to be on guard"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ahora eres un no fumador y estás tratando de mantenerte así. Cuando hacemos cambios, es fundamental meditar sobre cuán importante es este cambio para ti y cuán seguro te sientes al hacer este cambio. Debes prestar atención a cómo se siente tu mente, cuerpo y tu regulación emocional, cómo cambió tu actitud y qué has comenzado a hacer para cuidarte mejor.  Pensar en ello te ayuda a no retroceder a tu antigua relación con el cigarrillo.  Ahora sabes qué esperar en este viaje. No te tomará por sorpresa cuando tengas altibajos en este camino. Recuerda que todo se trata de idear una estrategia que funcione para ti, no de tu fuerza de voluntad.  ¿Ya estás fuera de peligro? Muchas personas quieren saber cuánto tiempo pasará para que la posibilidad de volver al tabaco deje de ser una preocupación. La recaída ocurre con más frecuencia en el primer mes a tres meses después de dejar de fumar.                                                                      Sin embargo, siempre es prudente estar alerta.\n               "
          }
        }
      }
    },
