    "NCM-4s-eAi.text" : {
      "comment" : "Class = \"UILabel\"; text = \"How is vaping (E-cigarettes) safer than tobacco?\"; ObjectID = \"NCM-4s-eAi\";",
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "How is vaping (E-cigarettes) safer than tobacco?"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "¿Cómo es que vapear (cigarrillos electrónicos) es más seguro que fumar tabaco?\n"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ngd-6u-Bee.text" : {
      "comment" : "Class = \"UILabel\"; text = \"Approximately 75% of smokers want to quit, but 25% are not interested. Perhaps you are thinking about it, but not quite ready to act. Although, cigarettes are expensive, you might still like the sensations of smoking. You may also feel pressured to quit because people smoke on the break or you live with someone who also smokes.\\n\\nBut just so you know, thinking about quitting is already a first big step forward toward change! It’s normal to feel intimidated by taking action. No one wants to fail.. But think about this.. If it’s going to be a challenge now and it’s going to be a challenge in 5 years, why not do it now without spending more money on cigarettes?\"; ObjectID = \"Ngd-6u-Bee\";",
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Approximately 75% of smokers want to quit, but 25% are not interested. Perhaps you are thinking about it, but not quite ready to act. Although, cigarettes are expensive, you might still like the sensations of smoking. You may also feel pressured to quit because people smoke on the break or you live with someone who also smokes.\n\nBut just so you know, thinking about quitting is already a first big step forward toward change! It’s normal to feel intimidated by taking action. No one wants to fail.. But think about this.. If it’s going to be a challenge now and it’s going to be a challenge in 5 years, why not do it now without spending more money on cigarettes?"
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Aproximadamente el 75% de los fumadores quieren dejarlo, pero el 25% no está interesado. Quizás estás pensando en ello, pero no estás del todo listo para actuar. Aunque los cigarrillos son caros, todavía disfrutas de fumar. También puedes sentirte presionado porque la gente a tu alrededor fuma en los breaks del trabajo o vives con alguien que también fuma.  Pero para que lo sepas, pensar en dejarlo ya es un primer gran paso hacia el cambio. Es normal sentirse intimidado. Nadie quiere fallar. Pero piensa en esto: si va a ser un desafío hoy y también será un desafío en 5 años, ¿por qué no hacerlo ahora sin gastar más dinero en cigarrillos?\n\n"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "nIg-1K-rx9.text" : {
      "comment" : "Class = \"UILabel\"; text = \"\\\"Drug use\\\" refers to\\n \\n1. the use of prescribed or over-the-counter drugs in excess of the directions, and \\n2. any non medical use of drugs.\\n\\nThe various classes of drugs may include cannabis (marijuana, hashish), solvents (e.g., paint thinner), tranquilizers (e.g., valium), barbiturates, cocaine, stimulants (e.g., speed), hallucinogens (e.g., LSD) or narcotics (e.g., heroin). The questions do not include alcoholic beverages.\\n\\nPlease answer the questions in this survey. If you have difficulty with a statement, simply choose the best response possible.\\n\\nThese questions refer to drug use in the past 12 months. Please answer NO or YES to each question.\"; ObjectID = \"nIg-1K-rx9\";",
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "\"Drug use\" refers to\n \n1. the use of prescribed or over-the-counter drugs in excess of the directions, and \n2. any non medical use of drugs.\n\nThe various classes of drugs may include cannabis (marijuana, hashish), solvents (e.g., paint thinner), tranquilizers (e.g., valium), barbiturates, cocaine, stimulants (e.g., speed), hallucinogens (e.g., LSD) or narcotics (e.g., heroin). The questions do not include alcoholic beverages.\n\nPlease answer the questions in this survey. If you have difficulty with a statement, simply choose the best response possible.\n\nThese questions refer to drug use in the past 12 months. Please answer NO or YES to each question."
          }
        }
      }
    },
