    "q3Z-vg-55f.text" : {
      "comment" : "Class = \"UILabel\"; text = \"Many people think smoking relieves stress. However, Nicotine does something interesting in your brain – it releases a chemical called dopamine. Dopamine is like a happiness signal and makes you feel good. Some people with depression have low levels of dopamine, so they might smoke to get a quick boost. \\n\\nBut here's the problem... once your brain gets used to nicotine boosters, it will cry for more smoking when it is not getting enough nicotine. Thus, your concentration goes down, your heart beats faster, and you get more anxious and stressed.\\n\\nAs a result, you smoke to reduce your nicotine stress, not your real stress. This is a vicious cycle that affects your anxiety and mood.\\n\\nDepression is common because when you smoke a lot, your brain kind of switches off its own way of making dopamine. So, in the long run, your brain has less dopamine that affects your mood.\"; ObjectID = \"q3Z-vg-55f\";",
      "extractionState" : "extracted_with_value",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Many people think smoking relieves stress. However, Nicotine does something interesting in your brain – it releases a chemical called dopamine. Dopamine is like a happiness signal and makes you feel good. Some people with depression have low levels of dopamine, so they might smoke to get a quick boost. \n\nBut here's the problem... once your brain gets used to nicotine boosters, it will cry for more smoking when it is not getting enough nicotine. Thus, your concentration goes down, your heart beats faster, and you get more anxious and stressed.\n\nAs a result, you smoke to reduce your nicotine stress, not your real stress. This is a vicious cycle that affects your anxiety and mood.\n\nDepression is common because when you smoke a lot, your brain kind of switches off its own way of making dopamine. So, in the long run, your brain has less dopamine that affects your mood."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Muchas personas creen que fumar alivia el estrés. Sin embargo, la nicotina hace algo interesante en tu cerebro: libera una sustancia química llamada dopamina. La dopamina es como una señal de felicidad y te hace sentir bien. Algunas personas con depresión tienen niveles bajos de dopamina, por lo que podrían fumar para obtener un impulso rápido.\n\r\nPero aquí está el problema… una vez que tu cerebro se acostumbra a los estímulos de la nicotina, pedirá más cigarrillos cuando no reciba suficiente nicotina. Así, tu concentración disminuye, el corazón late más rápido, y te sientes más ansioso y estresado.\n\r\nComo resultado, fumas para reducir el estrés causado por la falta de nicotina, no tu estrés real. Este es un círculo vicioso que afecta tu ansiedad y estado de ánimo.\n\r\nLa depresión es común porque, cuando fumas mucho, tu cerebro prácticamente apaga su propia manera de producir dopamina. A largo plazo, tu cerebro produce menos dopamina, lo cual afecta tu estado de ánimo.\n "
          }
        }
      }
    },
